# Generated API docs

The [generated API reference](https://benomahony.github.io/zig-typesafe-ai/api/)
lists every public declaration with its doc comment. To build it locally with
Zig's autodoc:

```sh
zig build docs
python3 -m http.server -d zig-out/docs/api
```

# How the examples are tested

Every Zig example in these docs, the README and the doc comments is quoted from
a region of a test, marked like this:

```
// docs:start NAME
...
// docs:end NAME
```

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `zig build test` | Offline: unit tests, compiles the e2e tests and the consumer project, and fails if any snippet is stale or any Zig code in the docs isn't quoted from a test |
| `TYPESAFE_API_KEY=... zig build e2e` | Runs the e2e tests and the quick start against the live API |
| `zig build snippets` | Re-extracts the snippets after you edit a test |

The snippets come from:

- `tests/e2e.zig`: end-to-end tests. Assertions sit outside the quoted
  regions, and check ranges and unambiguous cases rather than exact model
  output.
- `tests/consumer/`: a downstream project that depends on `tai` by path.
  Its `build.zig` is the install example, and its `main.zig` is the quick start.

# Examples

The `examples/` directory contains three runnable programs. Each needs
`TYPESAFE_API_KEY`.

| Command | Shows |
| --- | --- |
| `zig build run-triage -- "message"` | The typed DSL end to end |
| `zig build run-dynamic -- "text" label...` | Runtime-built questions with `systemOne` |
| `zig build run-models` | `listModels` |

# Mapping to the HTTP API

| HTTP | tai |
| --- | --- |
| `POST /v1/systemone` | `Client.ask` (typed) and `Client.systemOne` (runtime) |
| `GET /v1/models` | `Client.listModels` |
| `Authorization: Bearer` | `Options.api_key` / `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` |
| `state` | The first argument of `ask`, or `Request.state` |
| `questions.{id}` | A struct field name, or `NamedQuestion.name` |
| noul `criteria.true` / `.false` | `.criteria(yes, no)` |
| choice `criteria` map | Struct literal or enum type |
| score `criteria` array | Tuple, struct literal, or enum type |
| `answers.{id}` | `r.answers.{field}` or `Response.get(id)` |
| `usage` | `r.usage` |
